ityQualifier":null,"alternatives":null,"selectedAlternative":null,"optional":null}}],"steps":[{"n":1,"text":"Wash blood and organs off of all the chicken parts.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":2,"text":"Bring chicken and water to a simmer, skim, and add ice. Skim the fat that's consolidated by the ice.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":3,"text":"Add the rest of the ingredients, simmer for 40 minutes, then rest for 10 minutes.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":4,"text":"Gently strain stock so as to not push impurities through mesh.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":5,"text":"Bring back to heat and cook down to 4 ½ quarts.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":6,"text":"Fill a wide pot with salted water and bring to simmer.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":7,"text":"Combine water, butter, and 1 tsp of salt in a medium saucepan; bring to simmer.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":8,"text":"Add flour and cook on medium for about 5 minutes, bringing out a nutty aroma, but being careful not to brown.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":9,"text":"Put dough in mixing bowl, add mustard and salt, and start mixing on low speed.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":10,"text":"Add eggs one at a time, beating until incorporated. Add chives.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":11,"text":"Make quenelles from the dough with two spoons, and cook for about 7 minutes in the large pot of salted water. Rest on cutting board.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":12,"text":"Melt the butter on low heat.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":13,"text":"Add vegetables and salt, then cook on low heat for 30–35 minutes, covered with a parchment lid.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":14,"text":"Add the stock, and simmer for 30 minutes. Strain out the vegetables and discard.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":15,"text":"Whisk in the roux, a little at a time, and simmer for 30 minutes, skimming out impurities. Use enough roux to thicken to your preference.","durationMinutes":null},{"n":16,"text":"Blanche the celery in salted water until tender, then cool in ice bath.",